{
  "_comment": [
    "The rules both implementations of the note prompt's post-conditions are built from.",
    "",
    "research/prompts/checks.py reads this file. backend/src/ScreenTail.Api/Summarize/DraftValidator.cs",
    "keeps the same values as constants, so the service has no file to load at startup, and",
    "SharedRulesTests in the backend suite fails when the two differ. hardening-cases.json says what",
    "the rules must answer; this file says what they are. The 2026-10-12 review found the server's key",
    "shapes and cue words narrower than the client's pattern library, and the two validators each",
    "claiming to mirror the other is how that happened.",
    "",
    "Every pattern has to mean the same thing to .NET and to Python's re module, so nothing here uses",
    "\\p{...}, named groups or variable-width lookbehind; a scoped flag such as (?i:...) means the same",
    "in both. key_shapes and the cue words are kept at",
    "least as broad as client/ScreenTail.Core/Privacy/PatternLibrary.cs, and",
    "research/tests/test_shared_rules.py reads that file to notice when it learns a shape this one",
    "does not have."
  ],
